<h2>Avon Science Fiction and Fantasy Reader</h2>
When Donald Wollheim left Avon in 1952, they decided to combine <i>Avon
Fantasy Reader</i> and <i>Avon Science Fiction Reader</i> into a new quarterly,
<i>Avon Science Fiction and Fantasy Reader</i>. Sol Cohen was supposed to edit
the new quarterly with a portfolio of brand new stories. However, the
enterprise promptly collapsed after only two issues, partially because
many stories were not exactly top-notch.

